  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1240 PM MDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nTemperatures will warm a bit on Wednesday, hovering around seasonal \naverages. Meanwhile, some upsloping into the southeast mountains \nwill continue, helping keep a bit of moisture in our region. \nHowever, the majority of the large-scale forcing will move south and \neast of our CWA, taking a good amount of our precip chances with it. \nFor Wednesday afternoon, isolated showers and thunderstorms will be \npossible over the southeast mountains, while some scattered showers \nwill be possible over the Pikes Peak area, Raton Mesa/southern \nSangres, and portions of the eastern San Juans. Otherwise, the rest \nof our area will remain mostly dry.\n\nLooking towards the end of the week, high pressure begins to build \nin across the region once more. Hotter and drier conditions will \nresume dominating SE Colorado, with highs back in the 90s. While a \nfew isolated afternoon showers will be possible, the area will also \nlargely remain dry. This trend looks to persist into this weekend, \nwith temps over the plains climbing back into the triple digits.",
